fried fish eggplant and potato patties  in the old town of Rabat visitors are  tempted by a wide variety of Moroccan  delicacies fine food plays an important  role in the North African country and  much of it is homemade the fish is  freshly caught from the ocean the silver  fish factory near Casablanca is one of  the country's largest it employs around  1,000 people who process sardines about  60% of it is exported the products are  sold under various brand names the Nixa  brand name is made for the German market  and is certified this certification  allows us to sell our products in the  European and international markets we're  certified eco-friendly products are  worth more but the certification has no  influence on prices here in Morocco the  domestic market is also important  Moroccans call sardines the poor man's  fish one kilo goes for less than 2 euros  some 40% of Moroccans work in  agriculture or the fishing industry but  experts warn of overfishing fish  production plays a key role in the  national economy and it has a future but  we can't allow ourselves to concentrate  solely on fishing because resources are  limited at some point these natural  resources will be depleted  fish production is an important sector  for Morocco annual sales total some 1  billion euros and that's set to triple  by 2020 so an appearance at Berlin's  green week comes just at the right  moment
 

